? Which sequence matches the PDF's four broad multimedia-development stages?
+ Planning/costing → designing/producing → testing → delivering
- Designing/producing → delivering → planning/costing → testing
- Testing → planning/costing → delivering → designing/producing
- Delivering → testing → designing/producing → planning/costing
= Start from purpose and resources, create the title, verify it, then deliver it. Feedback can lead to another cycle.

? What does project scope define when planning a multimedia title?
+ The boundaries of included work and practical constraints
- The colour values of every pixel in the final title
- The complete record of every user's future navigation
- The final audio volume for each individual speaker
= Scope sets boundaries such as included content, time, skills and organisation. It keeps the project manageable.

? Which set belongs in audience analysis for a learning title?
+ Language, prior knowledge and technological background
- Colour depth, aspect ratio and compression ratio
- File extension, folder name and export timestamp
- Timeline length, render speed and processor model
= Audience analysis asks who the users are. The PDF also lists age, gender, economic background and profession.

? Which team member primarily integrates prepared assets into a working multimedia application?
+ Multimedia programmer
- Video specialist
- Audio specialist
- Printing operator
= The multimedia programmer uses an authoring system or programming language to connect assets and behaviour.

? What is the main purpose of a storyboard for an interactive multimedia title?
+ Sketch the content and appearance of its screens
- Measure the network speed of its delivery server
- Record only the completed title's sales revenue
- Replace all detailed scripts with a font catalogue
= A storyboard shows the planned screens or shots and helps turn the project's goals into a specification.

? What does a navigation map primarily show?
+ Routes linking screens or content components
- Every pixel's final display colour and location
- Every sound sample's amplitude and frequency
- A list of the operating system's device drivers
= Navigation mapping defines how users can move through the title; it may be combined with a logical-flow definition.

? Which script-writing practice does the PDF recommend for an educational exercise?
+ Give feedback for correct and incorrect choices
- Hide all feedback until the software is uninstalled
- Give feedback only when the answer is correct
- Replace feedback with an unrelated animation
= Both kinds of feedback support learning. The script should explicitly specify media, interaction and responses.

? A layout repeats the same heading and button treatment throughout a lesson. Which principle most directly explains this organised repetition?
+ Rhythm or pattern
- Random variation
- Colour quantisation
- Audio sampling
= Repeated elements create rhythm/pattern and can support balance and harmony.

? A designer deliberately makes the main instruction stronger than supporting detail. Which principle is being applied?
+ Hierarchy and emphasis
- File compression
- Font rasterization
- Network routing
= Hierarchy assigns priority; emphasis attracts attention to the important element.

? Which description best matches alpha testing in the PDF?
+ Early review of concept, interface and layout, often by the team
- Final release to the whole public with no recorded evaluation
- Removal of all test records after the software is distributed
- Recording only the volume and colour of imported media assets
= Alpha testing occurs earlier and can use a partly implemented title. Beta testing is near release with real users.

? Which authoring metaphor organises media instances in tracks with time running horizontally?
+ Cast, score and scripting
- Plain-text character coding
- Colour lookup table indexing
- Directory-based file compression
= The PDF uses Director and Lingo as examples of cast/score/scripting authoring.

? What should accompany delivery of a multimedia title?
+ Installation steps, requirements and troubleshooting guidance
- An internal asset inventory without installation or user guidance
- A complete design storyboard without a usable delivery package
- A production budget without any instructions for the target users
= Delivery includes a usable package and instructions for obtaining, installing and running it, including likely problems and solutions.
